David Damerell <damerell@chiark.greenend.org.uk> writes:

> Eva Myers  <erm1001@cam.ac.uk> wrote:
> >The confusing bit is that although I know that Demogorgon's first
> >sickness attack will leave you with between 20 and (19 + Con) turns to
> >live, and each subsequent attack will divide your time to live by 3
> >(rounding down) and then add 1, I'm not clear on how many moves the
> >player or Demogorgon will get during a "turn". 
> 
> If we assume that turns here are the underlying game turns, a "very fast"
> player will always get at least a third move in every pair of turns.
> 
> Demogorgon's speed is 15, with 12 being normal speed. This implies he will
> move twice every 3 turns on a regular cycle. If he were hasted, he would
> have speed 20, moving once-twice-once-twice-twice in a 5-turn cycle.
> 
> To be precise, a very fast player receives either 18 or 24 movement points
> every turn, the latter with probability 1/3, with 12 sufficing to make a
> move. The significant fact is that a very fast player, as mentioned above,
> will always get a double move the turn after they get a single move.

So monsters get their extra moves in a regular pattern, but players
get theirs at random?  And a monster with speed 20 is 8/5 as fast as a
monster with speed 12, not 5/3 as fast which you might expect?

> The status bar counter is in turns, and hence a vigilant player could work
> out whether they definitely had a double move coming up.
> 
> I _believe_ that even when both the player and some monsters will
> double-move, the sequence is still player-player-monster-monster.

The turn ends after the monster's move(s)?  That makes sense - after
all, if it ended after your move, you would never die from
Demogorgon's sickness without getting a chance to act.

If I've understood this correctly, then you can safely go two rounds
against Demogorgon before healing yourself, and sometimes a third.  Of
course, this ignores Demogorgon's ability to knock down your HP, as
well as the unreliability of some healing mechanisms.  Detailed
calculations follow:

If Demogorgon gets two moves in the first round:
Demogorgon stings!  Your time to live is now 20.
Demogorgon stings!  Your ttl = 7.
The turn ends.  Your ttl is now 6.

In the second round, his first sting knocks your ttl down to 3, and
the second sting (if there is one) reduces it to 2, bringing it to 2
or 1 after this turn ends.  At this point, any more stings will kill
you.

If Demogorgon only gets one move in the first round:
Demogorgon stings!  Your ttl is now 20.
The turn ends.  Your ttl is now 19.

One sting in the second round will take it down to 6, and as detailed
above, you can last another two-sting round before you urgently need
to heal.  Two stings in the second round, however, will take it down
to 2, and you will need to heal immediately.
